  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1:  A few gusty thunderstorms possible across \nportions of the Lower and Middle Susquehanna Valley this \nafternoon and evening.\n\nA weak upper level disturbance embedded in the NW flow aloft\nwill race SE and over a favorable zone of convergence along a\nlee trough that will be situated across the Middle and Lower\nSusq Valley this afternoon/early evening. \n\nSurface dewpoints in the low to mid 60s convergence and the\npassage of the left exit region of a 90 kt jet max over Ohio and\nSW PA late this afternoon will provide the fuel and favorable\nlarger scale UVVEL for some pulse and small clusters of \nstrong to potentially svr multicell TSRA across the I-81 and RT\n11/15 corridors in southern PA within a fairly narrow corridor\nof sfc-based CAPE between 1000-1500 J/KG between 18Z-00Z\ntoday/Monday. SPC has this relatively small portion of\nour CWA in a MRGL Risk for SVR TSRA today.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Turning more humid and unsettled early in the\nupcoming week with the highest probability for showers and \nthunderstorms Monday afternoon and evening and again on Tuesday \nand Tuesday night.\n\nA warm front will be moving across western PA Monday \nafternoon/evening, followed by a rather potent/digging mid/upper\nlevel shortwave and surface low. This shortwave will help to\namplify a slow-moving upper trough over the Mid Atlantic Region\nas we head into the midweek period.\n\nFcst dewpoints are not all that high for late July, and there \nhas been a slight downward trend with fcst dewpoints over the \nlast few days.\n\nMain things supporting showers and storms is a deepening low,\nand a large scale pattern that supports significant directional\nand speed shear in advance of a quite anomalous 995-1000 mb sfc\nlow moving over or just north of PA on Tuesday. Hodographs\nTuesday have a broad loop, but winds in the lowest KM are fairly\nlight, so we're leaning to the storm type being pulse, but with \n0-2KM helicity values peaking around 150 M2/S2 Tuesday, we could\nsee some transient supercells over Central and Ern PA during \nthe afternoon.\n\nPrevious disc...\n\nThe timing of the favorable lift associated with the thermally \nindirect, left front quad of the 80+ KT jet max moving across\nthe Ohio Valley, WVA and southern PA Tuesday afternoon and \nevening will help to enhance a low level lee trough and \nconvection along it. Scattered strong to severe TSRA are likely \nTue afternoon and evening over at least the eastern half of the\nCWA with a second line of TSRA likely along the cold front\nacross NW PA Tuesday afternoon.",
